⚠ POLICY CALL, NOT A MECHANICAL ONE.  This header lives only in the read-only
`mame` tree today; the overlay carries the .cpp but not the .h.  Adding it means
the overlay must keep a CPU header in sync with upstream.  The alternative is to
send the same four lines upstream.  Either way the change is additive and
default-inert: an unbound devcb write is a no-op, so ngp, namcos10 and every
other tmp95c061 consumer is unaffected.

